WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.246
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEIC preparation.

2
00:00:05.546 --> 00:00:08.932
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.232 --> 00:00:18.142
Unit sixteen: Part 7: Emails and Memos. Today you will read business emails and memos and answer detail and inference questions.

4
00:00:18.442 --> 00:00:20.990
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.933 --> 00:00:25.038
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:26.687
Memo.

7
00:00:27.683 --> 00:00:30.484
Memo means a short written message inside a company.

8
00:00:31.083 --> 00:00:32.026
Read the memo.

9
00:00:32.617 --> 00:00:34.897
Your turn. Say: Memo.

10
00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:38.607
Memo.

11
00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:40.328
Recipient.

12
00:00:41.317 --> 00:00:44.001
Recipient means the person who receives a message.

13
00:00:44.617 --> 00:00:46.535
The recipient is the manager.

14
00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:49.396
Your turn. Say: Recipient.

15
00:00:52.233 --> 00:00:53.304
Recipient.

16
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:54.877
Sender.

17
00:00:55.883 --> 00:00:58.394
Sender means the person who sends a message.

18
00:00:58.983 --> 00:01:00.542
The sender is Ms. Kim.

19
00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:03.152
Your turn. Say: Sender.

20
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.036
Sender.

21
00:01:07.783 --> 00:01:08.924
Attachment.

22
00:01:09.917 --> 00:01:12.369
Attachment means a file sent with an email.

23
00:01:12.983 --> 00:01:14.310
Open the attachment.

24
00:01:14.917 --> 00:01:17.325
Your turn. Say: Attachment.

25
00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:21.237
Attachment.

26
00:01:21.983 --> 00:01:23.008
Request.

27
00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:26.121
Request means asking for something.

28
00:01:26.717 --> 00:01:28.554
The email contains a request.

29
00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:32.151
Your turn. Say: Request.

30
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.117
Request.

31
00:01:36.883 --> 00:01:37.687
Mention.

32
00:01:38.683 --> 00:01:40.474
Mention means to say briefly.

33
00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:42.909
The email mentions a delay.

34
00:01:43.517 --> 00:01:45.739
Your turn. Say: Mention.

35
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:49.473
Mention.

36
00:01:50.217 --> 00:01:51.148
Not true.

37
00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:55.833
Not true means a NOT question: find the false option.

38
00:01:56.417 --> 00:01:57.778
Which is NOT true?

39
00:01:58.383 --> 00:02:00.873
Your turn. Say: Not true.

40
00:02:03.733 --> 00:02:05.164
Not true.

41
00:02:05.917 --> 00:02:06.883
Infer.

42
00:02:07.883 --> 00:02:11.253
Infer means to understand something not directly stated.

43
00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:13.780
You can infer the plan changed.

44
00:02:14.383 --> 00:02:16.386
Your turn. Say: Infer.

45
00:02:19.233 --> 00:02:20.327
Infer.

46
00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:24.656
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.517 --> 00:02:27.818
Visal, what is Part 7?

48
00:02:28.917 --> 00:02:43.179
It has fifty-four questions based on texts such as emails, memos, notices, ads, forms and message chains. It is the longest part, so time management is important.

49
00:02:44.283 --> 00:02:45.714
How do I read an email?

50
00:02:46.817 --> 00:02:59.512
Check the sender, recipient and subject line, then read the first and last sentences for the purpose and the request. Questions follow the order of the text in most cases.

51
00:03:00.617 --> 00:03:02.187
What are NOT questions?

52
00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:14.214
They ask which statement is not true or not mentioned. Check each option against the text, and eliminate those that are stated, until one is left.

53
00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:16.890
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:21.735
Grammar focus: Strategy: purpose, details, then answer.

55
00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:23.303
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:24.017 --> 00:03:27.142
Ms. Kim is writing to ask for a change to the schedule.

57
00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:31.887
Which is NOT true? Check each option and eliminate the true ones.

58
00:03:32.833 --> 00:03:39.721
Read the first and last sentences for the purpose, use keywords to find details, and check every option for NOT questions.

59
00:03:40.483 --> 00:03:44.633
Be careful! Don't say: I read the whole email word by word.

60
00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.168
Say: I find the purpose and keywords.

61
00:03:49.468 --> 00:03:50.667
Purpose first.

62
00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:54.340
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:56.564
A Business Email.

64
00:03:56.864 --> 00:03:59.398
Ms. Kim writes an email to the sales team.

65
00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.887
She says the Monday meeting will move to Wednesday.

66
00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:07.223
She attaches the new agenda and asks everyone to confirm.

67
00:04:08.233 --> 00:04:10.523
She also mentions that lunch will be provided.

68
00:04:11.533 --> 00:04:14.055
The email does not say who will lead the meeting.

69
00:04:15.167 --> 00:04:19.168
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:20.017 --> 00:04:22.074
How many questions are in Part 7?

71
00:04:22.374 --> 00:04:25.842
A, thirty. B, fifty-four. C, ten.

72
00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.759
The answer is B: fifty-four.

73
00:04:32.917 --> 00:04:35.137
What does Ms. Kim ask people to do?

74
00:04:35.437 --> 00:04:38.881
A, cancel. B, pay. C, confirm.

75
00:04:42.433 --> 00:04:44.514
The answer is C: confirm.

76
00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:47.150
The meeting moves to blank.

77
00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:51.092
A, Wednesday. B, Friday. C, Monday.

78
00:04:54.633 --> 00:04:56.610
The answer is A: Wednesday.

79
00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:59.308
What is NOT in the email?

80
00:04:59.608 --> 00:05:04.295
A, the agenda. B, who leads the meeting. C, the new date.

81
00:05:07.833 --> 00:05:10.576
The answer is B: who leads the meeting.

82
00:05:11.717 --> 00:05:13.507
For NOT questions, you blank.

83
00:05:13.807 --> 00:05:18.738
A, choose any option. B, skip them. C, eliminate true options.

84
00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:25.031
The answer is C: eliminate true options.

85
00:05:26.233 --> 00:05:29.791
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:32.731
How do you read an email in Part 7?

87
00:05:41.517 --> 00:05:43.075
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:59.776
I check the sender, the recipient and the subject, then read the first and last sentences to find the purpose and the request. I find details with keywords. For a NOT question, I check every option against the text.

89
00:06:00.076 --> 00:06:01.716
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:02.617 --> 00:06:07.997
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: purpose, details, then answer.

91
00:06:08.297 --> 00:06:12.424
Today's value is time management. Plan your day and use your time well.

92
00:06:12.724 --> 00:06:15.702
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:16.002 --> 00:06:18.433
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

